# Integration coverage exceptions (#167).
#
# `make integration-test` holds every package to the 90% integration-coverage
# floor (scripts/pkgtest.sh integration). This file names the only code
# excepted from that floor. Unit coverage has no exceptions: every file below
# is still covered by its unit tests and fixtures, which `make coverage` holds
# to the same 90%.
#
# One entry per line, four fields separated by " | ":
#
#   path | category | reason | approval
#
# path is a Go file, whose statements are left out of its package's integration
# coverage, or a package directory ending in "/", which is exempt from the
# integration floor: its coverage is still measured and reported, and never
# fails the gate. category is one of:
#
#   hardware       needs a device the devcontainer does not have
#   host-hardware  reaches what the host's hardware allows, so the same suite
#                  covers different amounts on different runners
#   host           would have to modify the host to reach
#   gui            needs a desktop session
#   defensive      branches no well-behaved client, peer or host produces
#                  (refusals of malformed input, write failures, kernel output
#                  that does not occur), all unit-covered
#   test-helper    ships nothing; exists only for tests
#
# An entry is added only with the owner's approval, recorded in its last field.
# Keep the list as small as the evidence allows.

